# Workbench Engineering Entry

Always load and follow `AGENTS.md` as the repository-wide canonical engineering source.
Engineering truth: `AGENTS.md` -> `docs/engineering/` -> file-scoped `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.
Business truth: current task -> confirmed PRD/decision -> implementation evidence.

## Mandatory Rules

- Monolith layer boundaries: Handler -> Service -> Repo -> Database. Handlers handle HTTP protocol; Services own business rules and object-level authorization; Repos own query building. Handlers MUST NOT touch DB; Repos MUST NOT decide permissions.
- Branch protection: Never write on `main` or `master`. Never create, switch, or rebase branches unless explicitly requested.
- Scope discipline: Only modify files within the allowed scope of the current task. Preserve unrelated dirty/untracked WIP.
- Schema ownership: Workbench-owned tables follow Workbench audit/soft-delete conventions; ZenTao tables follow legacy ZenTao schema. Do not invent schema without real DDL.
- Query standards: List queries follow SQL filter -> SQL sort -> SQL count -> SQL pagination. Never use `SELECT *` or large-table memory pagination.
- Pre-handoff gates:
  ```sh
  git diff --check
  make check
  ```
